1. What is ASU (Auto StartUp) ?
-------------------------------

Auto StartUp is an automatic application launcher.

2. Who would benefits from ASU ?
--------------------------------

You will benefit from ASU if you:
- own a Psion 5
- do daily/weekly backups
- need to start up utilities (eg.  Startup Plus, Remapper,
etc) after each backup

You may not want to install ASU if you:
- own a Psion 3A, 3C, 3MX, Sienna
- backup occasionally    
- do not need to startup utilities after each backup
- use the Psion 5 for specialised applications and do not use
any built-in applications

3. What ASU do for you ?
------------------------

ASU is a utility software that will help you re-open all your
non-builtin applications (built-in eg.  Word, Sheet)
AUTOMATICALLY.

There are several application launchers available as freeware
on the internet.  They can launch your applications but you
have to invoke these application launchers manually after a
Psiwin backup.

ASU does not replace these application launchers. ASU will
monitor your backup and automatically start these application
launchers to re-open your other favourite utilities. ASU does
not re-open your utilities directly.  (When I develop ASU, I
did not want to redo all the work that has been done by
others.)

Currently, only StartUp V2.00 is supported.

4. What benefits does ASU brings me ?
-------------------------------------

- allows you to backup more regularly (and with less hassle)
to ensure the the vital information in your Psion 5 is
protected
- ensures that all your utilities are ready to be used when
you need them and not waste previous time waiting for them to
start
- saves you the trouble in remembering all your useful
utiities which you need to re-open after a backup

5. IMPT Note !!
---------------

In order for ASU to function properly, you need to have at
least 1 built-in application open before backup.  These are:

Word  Sheet  Data  Agenda  Sketch  Program  Comms  Record

