8. Pre-requisite Software
-------------------------

You need to have a application launcher in your Psion 5.
Currently, ASU is design to work with:
- StartUp V2.00 by Philipp R. Salvisbery (http://salvis.com)

If you use other application launchers, either switch to
StartUp V2.00 or write me a note with the Website URL for me
to take a look.  If time permits, I will support these    
launchers but no guarantees.

9. Installation
---------------

After downloading the software, install it as any other SIS
file, ie from the folder that contains the SIS file:
- click on it to run the installation program and follow the
instructions given.

IMPT!!: Without running ASU, do a backup first.  This make
sure that the ASU program is backed up in your PC.  Otherwise,
when you later start ASU, you will keep getting a message that
tells you that ASU is opened.

Note that ASU currently resides only on C Disk and it assumes
that the application launcher also resides on C Disk.

If you have not installed any application launchers, please
get a copy from http://salvis.com and install it. It is a
freeware.

10. Configuring ASU
-------------------

To configure ASU, press the space bar to access the MENU when
there is no backing up activity.  The MENU does not work when
you are backing up your machine.

There are 2 options: 

- select the application launcher or none (for debugging
purposes)
- quit.  (Wrong place to have this option.)  Another way to
quit is to press Shift-Ctrl-Fn-K when you are in the ASU
program (warning: if you press Shift-Ctrl-Fn-K in the system
screen, you will reset the whole Psion 5.  This is a Psion 5      
feature not ASU.)

Please exit the MENU before you perform a backup.  ASU will
not be able to monitor your backups while you are in MENU.

11. Configuring StartUp V2.00 by Philipp R. Salvisberg
------------------------------------------------------

Before you use ASU, you need to configure StartUp V2.00 so
that it will launch the applications when it starts up and
then exit all by itself without user intervention.

Although the feature is available, I don't see the
documentation stating this.  Please "play around" a little
with StartUp V2.00.  You should be able to configure this
after a while.

12. What possible can go wrong & steps to resolve it
----------------------------------------------------

1. ASU detects starting of backup but does not detect backup
completion

No built-in applications open before backup. Click on the Word
icon. ASU will think that the backup has completed.

2. Backup fail to compete (disconnected)

Sometimes, the backup process itself can be accidentally
terminated, eg the cable is half-way disconnected. In this
situation, it is likely that all your built-in applications
have been close.
- if you do not want to resume the backup immediately, start
any built-in application to signal to ASU that backup has
completed.
- if you want to resume backup immediately, remember to
manually open at least one of the built-in applications after
the backup.  ASU will then start your application launcher.

3. The application launcher does not run

- Did you configure ASU not to run any utility or run the
wrong utility ?  Go to ASU, press space bar and check
- Did you install the application launcher on C Disk ?

4. StartUp V2.00 specific:  StartUp V2.00 runs but does not
launch your applications or does not quit after launching   

Read "Configuring StartUp V2.00 by Philipp R. Salvisberg"

5. Others:

- did you install ASU on C Disk ?
- did you install your application launcher on C Disk ?

